  "description": "VASP thermodynamic stability analysis workflow for crystalline materials. Automates the full pipeline: query Materials Project for competing phases, generate unified VASP inputs (POSCAR/INCAR/KPOINTS/POTCAR), submit HPC calculations (relaxation + static), extract energies, and build convex hull phase diagram to calculate energy above hull (ehull) and formation energy. Use this skill when the user mentions thermodynamic stability, convex hull, ehull, formation energy, competing phases, phase diagram, stability verification, or wants to assess whether a compound is thermodynamically stable using DFT/VASP calculations. Also triggers for queries about Materials Project phase analysis, pymatgen PhaseDiagram usage in stability context, or batch VASP calculation setup for multiple competing phases.",
